{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And He dealt well, etc. And the people multiplied, etc.</b> One needs to examine what the kindness was, and perhaps it is what is listed immediately afterward: ״וַיַּעַשׂ לָהֶם בָּתִּים״ — yet it is difficult, for if so, He would not have interrupted by saying ״וַיִּרֶב הָעָם״. It appears that Scripture informs us of a matter through whose instrumentality the children of Israel multiplied, in accordance with what has been set before us — that they supplied them with water and food. Therefore it says <b>וַיֵּיטֶב אֱלֹהִים לַמְיַלְּדֹת</b>, meaning, He gave them abundant good, and through it they had the means to supply food; and by this means <b>וַיִּרֶב הָעָם</b>, and without this they would not have been able to supply the multitudes in great abundance. Afterward HaShem mentioned their good reward — that He made them houses." "<b>Further</b>, it alludes that when HaShem saw their fear of Elohim, He brought within their grasp the performance of mitzvot without end, to multiply their reward. And that is what He says: <b>וַיֵּיטֶב</b>, etc., and what is the goodness? — <b>וַיִּרֶב הָעָם</b>, for through this their merit grows great, since all of them are accounted to them as though they had not killed them. Or perhaps, for this reason Moshe and Aharon merited leading Israel, for through them they merited, on one hand, because Yocheved and Miriam risked their lives for us and transgressed the king's command; and furthermore, they nourished and sustained them from their own resources — therefore they are accounted concerning Him: הוּא אָבִינוּ הוּא מַלְכֵּנוּ הוּא מוֹשִׁיעֵנוּ. And this also follows the same path, that since we are branches of the soul of Moshe, as it is written (Isaiah 63:11) ״מֹשֶׁה עַמּוֹ״ — therefore Yocheved bore our burden to shield us and to supply water and food, according to the way of mothers toward their children." "And according to the words of the commentators (Rashi) that the kindness was the making of the houses, one may say that the reason He interrupted by saying <b>וַיִּרֶב הָעָם</b> is that without this there would be no place for houses of priesthood and houses of royalty, for if there is no people there is no king and no priest. Therefore HaShem gave precedence to the people, and afterward made them houses, etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:23:32.712045923Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}